<Base title="Privacy and Browser Storage" description="How FreeJapaneseAcademy stores learning progress on your device and how to export or delete it." breadcrumbs={[{label:'Privacy',href:'/privacy/'}]}>
  <article class="prose-page"><span class="eyebrow">YOUR DATA</span><h1>Privacy & browser storage</h1><p>Last updated: November 1, 2026</p><h2>Progress on your device</h2><p>FreeJapaneseAcademy currently has no student account system. If you mark a lesson complete, bookmark a lesson, or take a demonstration quiz, that information is stored in your browser using IndexedDB. It is not automatically uploaded to a learning account or synchronized across devices.</p><h2>What's stored</h2><p>Your browser may store lesson identifiers and completion times, quiz results and timestamps, bookmarks, and settings you choose. You can view, export, import, or erase this data from the <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard/">dashboard</a>.</p><h2>Backups and clearing browser data</h2><p>Browser storage can be erased when you clear site data, use certain private browsing modes, or remove your browser profile. Export a JSON backup if you want to keep your progress. Imported files remain on your device and are validated before they replace existing progress.</p><h2>Hosting and technical requests</h2><p>The website is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Like other websites, the hosting infrastructure processes requests needed to deliver pages. This page describes the application's browser-side learning data; it does not imply that infrastructure request logs or browser networking data do not exist. A fuller privacy notice should be reviewed before adding analytics, accounts, or other third-party integrations.</p><h2>Questions and updates</h2><p>This privacy explanation will be updated as new features are added. For now, no external account or personal profile is needed to use the demonstration tools.</p></article>
</Base>
